 "notes": "top-torus-cover-winding is the flagship topology plate: fundamental square + torus ring + winding sequence γ(t)=[2t,−t] → lift (2,−1) + π₁ ≅ ℤ×ℤ, χ=0. Cymatic material is native where records are about resonance (ratio threshold, whole-tone return, foundational ratios, musical resolution, cymatics): cymatic entities carry template frequencies matched to the worked Hz scales (240/320/360/480; 288/384/432/576; n=1,2,3 modes at 110/220/330), with field resonator frequency/excitation raised only there. har-tetraktys-triangle carries an authored ASCII tetraktys. Metonic keeps the approximation sign load-bearing; cymatics keeps the 8+4 anchor mapping Offered with its discriminating test.  Cover note: tools/capture.mjs captures the active (first) scene, so the cover shows the opening projective-completion scene rather than the torus plate; the torus plate is captured per-scene in the draft review set (/tmp/roz-e4-drafts2, E4 session evidence).",
 "description": "Topology (projective completion/line, Riemann sphere, torus-cover-winding, Möbius-Klein, toroidal-poloidal, manifold atlas) and harmonics (whole-tone return, comma, cycle, musical resolution, Metonic, cymatics, perfect six, tetraktys).",
